## Data Layer

### Identity data

Name, email, phone, address, avatar, headline live in `user_profiles`. This table is shared across ALL roles. Never duplicate identity in role-specific or block tables.

### Block data

All role-specific data (CDL, employment, MVR, GitHub, etc.) lives in `block_*` tables. Reads and writes go through `src/lib/block-data.ts`.

See `.cursor/rules/block-development.mdc` for the full data architecture, including banned tables and the block data cheat sheet.

### API route pattern

```typescript
// GOOD — use block-data.ts helpers
import { getCdlData, saveCdlData } from '@/lib/block-data'
const cdl = await getCdlData(supabase, userId)
await saveCdlData(supabase, userId, { cdl_number: '...' })

// BAD — direct table queries from routes
const { data } = await supabase.from('block_driver_cdl').select('*')...
```

